<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS/CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS/CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and close of play scores on</p>
<p>the third day of four-day English county championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Saturday:</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham beat Derbyshire by six wickets.</p>
<p>Derbyshire 254 and 176. Durham 174 and 257-4 (J.Lewis 160 not</p>
<p>out, J.Boiling 62). Durham 20 points Derbyshire 6.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Warwickshire beat Sussex by nine wickets.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 227 and 41-1. Sussex 63 and 203 (C.Athey 67;</p>
<p>A.Donald 4-40). Warwickshire 21 points Sussex 4.</p>
<p>At Worcester: Worcestershire 422 (D.Leatherdale 129) Kent</p>
<p>235-7 (M.Ealham 56).</p>
<p>At Colchester: Essex 533-8 declared. Leicestershire 316-6</p>
<p>(I.Sutcliffe 130, N.Johnson 91; P.Such 4-55).</p>
<p>At Colwyn Bay: Nottinghamshire 202 and 6-0. Glamorgan 353-6</p>
<p>declared (S.James 162).</p>
<p>At Headingley: Yorkshire 166 and 332 (C.White 67, R.Blakey</p>
<p>51; R.Bailey 4-10). Northamptonshire 286 and 78-1.</p>
</text>
